    "result_text": "The build succeeds with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily registration limit rule: creating an owner is rejected with **429 Too Many Requests** once 100 or more owners already have today's registration date.\n\nFollowing the OfficeFloor function-injection pattern in this repo (mirroring the existing `EnsureCityCapacity` rule), I added:\n\n1. **`EnsureDailyRegistrationLimit`** (`rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 a pipeline step that counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()` and throws when the count reaches 100. It runs before the owner is saved, so the count excludes the owner being created (100 succeed, the 101st is rejected).\n\n2. **`DailyRegistrationLimitException`** (`rest/escalation/`) \u2014 a checked exception carrying the date and count.\n\n3. **`DailyRegistrationLimitExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds with `HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` (429) and a `ProblemDetail` body, matching the other escalation handlers.\n\n4. **Escalation YAML** wiring the exception to its handler.\n\n5. **Wired the step** into `owners.POST.yml` after `ensureCityCapacity` (with `govern: [ transaction ]` like the neighbouring checks), before `build`.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` passes (creates 100 owners dated today, then expects the 101st to be `429`), and the full suite is green.",
